   "source": [
    "<h3>CMS pileup data compression based on VQ-VAE compression</h3>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Experiment comments and insights:\n",
    "* Codebook entries from 256 vectors (rows), only approximately 120 codebook entries are used effectively based perplexity\n",
    "* Reconstruction improves with bigger latent vector and num embeddings. Reducing codebook size, improves usage but not reconstruction quality\n",
    "* Validation set properly works with higher beta coeficient roughly from beta in [0.2, 0.31]\n",
    "* Codebook plots describe codebook variation, whether certain weights are mostly zero (grey color) and are codebook usage is not sparse (orange colors)\n",
    "* Making encoded patch d > 2, we do not loose any information and perplexity does not collapse. When latent vector is flat, codebook usage is lower but not harms reconstruction"
   ]
  },
